When writing each chapter, it is necessary to list other related chapters.

The coordination content with the Electrical Discipline includes:
- Wall repair (Painting and patching) in the Architectural Discipline, which involves repairing and repainting walls damaged during the installation of electrical conduits;
- Firestopping, which requires sealing cable trays or conduits passing through firewalls with fire-resistant materials;
- And coordination items with the Architectural Discipline such as Elevators.

For the Mechanical Discipline, the related chapters include:
- Division 23 (HVAC systems);
- Division 25 (Plumbing systems), etc.

