The mechanical content related to the Electrical Discipline mainly includes:  
- Electrical heating in Division 14;  
- HVAC control systems (Electric and Electronic Control System for HVAC);  
- Building automation systems (BAS), also known as Energy Management Control Systems (EMCS), which are also coordination items.  

When referencing, only the chapter number and name need to be cited; specific content does not need to be referenced.  

The specific method for drafting specifications is typically handled by senior personnel. Although we cannot elaborate in detail here, we can outline the composition of each section. Generally, it is divided into three parts:  

The first part is General, covering relevant standards and requirements;  

The second part is Products, specifying technical indicators and product requirements;
